# c4c5-ambig-decidable — the decision table (family contract in fixture.yaml; per-row intent below).
# id               | world           | patch | env | expect
# strike-resumable  = #329 has AGENT_STRIKE: + Resumable branch pushed: → decidable: emits C4/C5
#                     unit with work-branch; #330 beside it keeps its ordinary v2 + unit
# no-strike         = #329 has NO terminal comment (no AGENT_STRIKE:/AGENT_REPORT:), no live pod, quiet
#                     past C4C5_PERSIST_S; nothing merged into goal/1162-scan (recorded `[]`) and no
#                     origin fix/issue-329-* branch → ABANDONED: the plain c4c5-redispatch unit, no
#                     work-branch (RESUMABLE <empty>). Until the dead-ride limbo fix (2026-11-16,
#                     #3303/#3308) this row expected the HELD report (`no-strike.txt`, kept for the
#                     rows that still hold); the expectation moved, the world gained the two reads.
# block-class-wins  = the SAME strike-resumable world, with #330's body carrying a machine block
#                     `Class: build`: the block WINS over the `task/*` label in the C4/C5 class
#                     derivation (ADR-122 (3), homelab#1460), so its unit re-dispatches as `build`
strike-resumable | strike-resumable |       |      | strike-resumable
no-strike        | no-strike        |       |      | goal-abandoned
block-class-wins | strike-resumable |       |      | block-class-wins
# block-class-malformed = the SAME strike-resumable world, with #329's (the decidable goal child's) body
#                     carrying a block the parser REFUSES (`Nope: x`): the resumable path HOLDS — no
#                     unit, a ⛔ orphan line, a strike-held class row (rule #6; PR#1503's review found
#                     this sibling loop dispatching on the label instead). #330 keeps its ordinary unit.
block-class-malformed | strike-resumable |       |      | block-class-malformed
# strike-resumable-markdown = the SAME strike-resumable world, but #329's comment carries the
#                     finalizer's LIVE markdown shape: `**Resumable branch pushed:** \`<branch>\``
#                     + trailing prose. The extraction must anchor the match, strip the backticks
#                     and cut at the first whitespace — the bare branch name and nothing else
#                     (the pre-fix `sub(".*Resumable branch pushed:[ \t]*"; "")` was greedy up to
#                     the opening `**`, so the value was `** \`agent/<branch>\` — …` and word-split
#                     in the dispatch loop: the #1780 dispatch arrived carrying `work-branch=**`).
#                     Same expected stream as strike-resumable: the markdown is not the value.
strike-resumable-markdown | strike-resumable-markdown |       |      | strike-resumable
# strike-no-resumable = the SAME world, but #329's AGENT_STRIKE comment carries NO
#                     `Resumable branch pushed:` line at all: the extraction yields an EMPTY
#                     work-branch (no partial match, no `**`) and the issue is held as today.
strike-no-resumable | strike-no-resumable |       |      | no-strike
# report-resumable   = #329 has AGENT_REPORT: (deliberate stop) + Resumable branch pushed: →
#                     decidable: emits C4/C5 unit with work-branch. Same behaviour as the
#                     AGENT_STRIKE path — the finalizer writes the same line to both comment
#                     channels (FU-199 / homelab#1797, one parser). #330 keeps its ordinary unit.
report-resumable | report-resumable |       |      | report-resumable
# report-resumable-markdown = the SAME report-resumable world, but #329's comment carries the
#                     finalizer's LIVE markdown shape: `**Resumable branch pushed:** \`<branch>\``
#                     + trailing prose. Same extraction as strike-resumable-markdown (one parser,
#                     one reader for both AGENT_STRIKE and AGENT_REPORT, anchor the match, strip
#                     backticks, cut at first whitespace). Same expected stream as report-resumable.
report-resumable-markdown | report-resumable-markdown |       |      | report-resumable
# ── the no-terminal-record leg (dead-ride limbo, 2026-11-16): the merge evidence decides ──
# goal-abandoned-branch = no terminal comment; the merged PRs into goal/1162-scan come from OTHER
#                     heads (fix/issue-327-*, fix/issue-328-*) and neither cites #329 (one mentions
#                     "the goal's next child" in prose, no number); origin fix/issue-329-x is 1 ahead
#                     of the base → c4c5-redispatch carrying work-branch=fix/issue-329-x
#                     (RESUMABLE line). On master this world emits the HELD report.
goal-abandoned-branch | goal-abandoned-branch |       |      | goal-abandoned-branch
# goal-own-head-merged = CONTROL: a merged PR into the base whose HEAD is fix/issue-329-loop, body
#                     not citing #329 — the circles#36 shape (finished work, unlinked). Stays HELD,
#                     plus a ⛔ line naming the merged PR; no branch read, no unit for #329.
goal-own-head-merged | goal-own-head-merged |       |      | goal-own-head-merged
# goal-merged-probe-fail = the no-strike world, but the merged-PR read into the base FAILS: HELD,
#                     one PROBE_FAILED line (rule #6), no branch read, no unit for #329.
goal-merged-probe-fail | no-strike |       | STUB_GH_pr_list_merged=fail | goal-merged-probe-fail
# goal-refs-probe-fail = the no-strike world, but the origin-branch read FAILS: HELD, one
#                     PROBE_FAILED line — a resumable branch may exist, so no restart is guessed.
goal-refs-probe-fail | no-strike |       | STUB_GH_api_repos_teststuffstash_homelab_git_matching_refs_heads_fix_issue_329=fail | goal-refs-probe-fail
# goal-child-recent = the no-strike world, #329 touched "now": inside the C4C5_PERSIST_S guard the
#                     evidence is not read at all — the HELD stream byte-for-byte (`no-strike.txt`).
goal-child-recent | no-strike | gh/issue-list-inprog.json @ patches/goal-child-recent.jq |      | no-strike
